1
00:01:38,200 --> 00:01:44,030
[Small Town Remedy]

2
00:01:44,229 --> 00:01:46,720
[Episode 17]

3
00:01:46,970 --> 00:01:48,150
[Ambulance]

4
00:01:48,150 --> 00:01:49,240
[Fucheng Emergency Medical Rescue Center]

5
00:01:49,270 --> 00:01:52,880
[Ambulance]

6
00:01:59,560 --> 00:02:00,120
Come on.

7
00:02:02,200 --> 00:02:03,230
Careful. Careful.

8
00:02:03,230 --> 00:02:04,280
Move aside!

9
00:02:05,120 --> 00:02:06,310
Make way! Make way!

10
00:02:06,840 --> 00:02:07,710
Careful. This way.

11
00:02:07,710 --> 00:02:09,440
The patient's semiconscious.

12
00:02:09,840 --> 00:02:10,630
This way! This way!

13
00:02:10,630 --> 00:02:11,560
Let me take over.

14
00:02:12,120 --> 00:02:12,960
Careful. Careful.

15
00:02:12,960 --> 00:02:14,020
Careful. Careful.

16
00:02:24,910 --> 00:02:26,150
Sir, you want to talk?

17
00:02:26,400 --> 00:02:28,400
He wants to talk. Take it off for now.

18
00:02:32,310 --> 00:02:33,150
My son...

19
00:02:33,710 --> 00:02:35,150
Dad, I'm here. I'm here.

20
00:02:37,079 --> 00:02:38,840
I'm done for.

21
00:02:39,120 --> 00:02:39,870
Stop, Dad.

22
00:02:39,870 --> 00:02:40,680
Don't talk nonsense.

23
00:02:40,680 --> 00:02:41,960
Just relax.

24
00:02:42,360 --> 00:02:43,470
Look at this hospital,

25
00:02:43,470 --> 00:02:45,030
with all the high-tech equipment.

26
00:02:45,030 --> 00:02:46,840
And the doctors are all here.

27
00:02:46,870 --> 00:02:48,070
You won't be done for.

28
00:02:49,079 --> 00:02:50,520
Alright, that's enough.

29
00:02:50,680 --> 00:02:52,630
Sir, your blood oxygen level has dropped.

30
00:02:52,630 --> 00:02:54,079
It's okay. Don't worry.

31
00:02:54,079 --> 00:02:54,910
Your heart rate is a little high.

32
00:02:54,910 --> 00:02:55,870
Just relax,

33
00:02:55,870 --> 00:02:56,960
and your heart rate will go down.

34
00:02:56,960 --> 00:02:57,840
It's okay.

35
00:02:58,220 --> 00:02:59,930
[Priority for Patients with Acute Stroke]

36
00:02:58,710 --> 00:02:59,800
When the patient was brought in,

37
00:02:59,800 --> 00:03:01,360
his oxygen saturation was only 85%.

38
00:02:59,950 --> 00:03:01,470
[Priority for Seniors Aged 80 and Older]

39
00:03:01,400 --> 00:03:02,750
It could be a lung problem.

40
00:03:02,750 --> 00:03:03,800
85?

41
00:03:04,870 --> 00:03:06,560
That's a pretty good score.

42
00:03:06,800 --> 00:03:07,960
I told you
you didn't have to be that concerned.

43
00:03:07,040 --> 00:03:12,110
[Wishing You a Speedy Recovery]

44
00:03:08,680 --> 00:03:09,870
An oxygen saturation below 90%

45
00:03:09,870 --> 00:03:10,800
means hypoxemia.

46
00:03:10,800 --> 00:03:11,470
At 85%,

47
00:03:11,470 --> 00:03:12,750
it's already very serious.

48
00:03:12,180 --> 00:03:18,310
[Priority for Patients with Acute Stroke]

49
00:03:14,630 --> 00:03:16,230
I thought 0 was dangerous.

50
00:03:16,230 --> 00:03:16,400
Then...

51
00:03:16,400 --> 00:03:17,630
Just stop blabbering.

52
00:03:17,630 --> 00:03:19,120
Does the patient have any medical history?

53
00:03:19,120 --> 00:03:20,590
Has he taken any medication recently?

54
00:03:20,590 --> 00:03:22,590
He had a pulmonary embolism before.

55
00:03:23,079 --> 00:03:24,960
He's been taking warfarin ever since,

56
00:03:24,960 --> 00:03:26,760
I think that's what it's called.

57
00:03:27,000 --> 00:03:28,860
Then, about 2 weeks ago,

58
00:03:28,880 --> 00:03:30,470
he developed a fever and cough.

59
00:03:30,470 --> 00:03:31,590
The doctor in town said

60
00:03:31,590 --> 00:03:32,960
it was bronchitis,

61
00:03:33,150 --> 00:03:33,840
so he got

62
00:03:33,840 --> 00:03:35,079
IV drips for half a month,

63
00:03:35,079 --> 00:03:36,680
but they didn't seem to help.

64
00:03:37,079 --> 00:03:39,030
Then he took licorice tablets

65
00:03:39,360 --> 00:03:41,430
and some cough and phlegm medicine,

66
00:03:41,430 --> 00:03:43,490
but those didn't seem to help either.

67
00:03:44,590 --> 00:03:46,590
This doesn't look like simple bronchitis.

68
00:03:46,590 --> 00:03:48,079
Then what could it be?

69
00:03:49,120 --> 00:03:50,650
It should be a lung disease.

70
00:03:50,910 --> 00:03:51,630
But

71
00:03:51,870 --> 00:03:53,960
if it were ordinary pneumonia,

72
00:03:54,190 --> 00:03:55,610
antibiotics should've helped

73
00:03:55,610 --> 00:03:56,960
after 2 weeks of treatment.

74
00:03:56,960 --> 00:03:57,710
The patient's having trouble breathing!

75
00:03:57,710 --> 00:03:59,079
His oxygen saturation is below 70%,

76
00:03:59,079 --> 00:04:00,150
and his blood pressure is also dropping!

77
00:04:00,150 --> 00:04:00,910
Prepare for intubation,

78
00:04:00,910 --> 00:04:02,110
and get him to the ICU!

79
00:04:02,560 --> 00:04:03,120
Come on!

80
00:04:03,630 --> 00:04:04,830
Move aside! Make way!

81
00:04:08,680 --> 00:04:09,340
Be careful.

82
00:04:09,710 --> 00:04:10,280
Careful.

83
00:04:18,209 --> 00:04:21,839
[Family Visitation Window]

84
00:04:21,600 --> 00:04:23,360
This is really strange.

85
00:04:24,600 --> 00:04:25,800
Look at the chest CT.

86
00:04:27,680 --> 00:04:30,000
There's consolidation and exudation
in the right lower lobe,

87
00:04:30,000 --> 00:04:31,660
along with air bronchograms.

88
00:04:31,920 --> 00:04:33,780
Everything points to pneumonia.

89
00:04:34,630 --> 00:04:36,510
The township clinic started him
on ceftriaxone

90
00:04:36,510 --> 00:04:37,510
and azithromycin,

91
00:04:37,510 --> 00:04:38,920
then switched to minocycline,

92
00:04:38,920 --> 00:04:40,070
but none of them worked.

93
00:04:39,909 --> 00:04:44,250
[Infective Waste]

94
00:04:40,600 --> 00:04:42,070
Either the bacteria are drug-resistant,

95
00:04:42,070 --> 00:04:44,070
or it's not ordinary pneumonia.

96
00:04:44,600 --> 00:04:46,600
That's what makes this so puzzling.

97
00:04:47,070 --> 00:04:48,090
If it's not pneumonia,

98
00:04:48,090 --> 00:04:49,290
what else could it be?

99
00:04:50,159 --> 00:04:51,680
But how are we supposed to treat it

100
00:04:51,680 --> 00:04:53,409
if we can't identify the cause?

101
00:04:59,480 --> 00:05:00,270
Try this.

102
00:05:01,040 --> 00:05:03,100
You stewed the green beans yourself?

103
00:05:06,870 --> 00:05:07,870
So good!

104
00:05:08,630 --> 00:05:11,560
I always eat at the cafeteria,
and I'm getting sick of it.

105
00:05:11,560 --> 00:05:13,000
You really know how to cook green beans.

106
00:05:13,000 --> 00:05:13,560
Here,

107
00:05:14,830 --> 00:05:17,760
have some of this high-quality protein
to go with it.

108
00:05:18,600 --> 00:05:19,390
Thanks.

109
00:05:21,680 --> 00:05:23,800
At least have something to eat or drink.

110
00:05:23,800 --> 00:05:25,400
The food's going to get cold.

111
00:05:27,510 --> 00:05:28,570
I have no appetite.

112
00:05:30,240 --> 00:05:32,170
Worried about Mr. Wu's condition?

113
00:05:32,680 --> 00:05:33,310
Yes.

114
00:05:33,430 --> 00:05:34,490
It's a tricky case.

115
00:05:34,750 --> 00:05:35,570
Even Li and Jin

116
00:05:35,600 --> 00:05:37,600
can't figure out what's causing it.

117
00:05:38,190 --> 00:05:39,480
Didn't he have
a pulmonary embolism before?

118
00:05:39,480 --> 00:05:40,240
Could it be

119
00:05:40,240 --> 00:05:41,310
another one?

120
00:05:43,480 --> 00:05:45,630
He does have a history of
pulmonary embolism,

121
00:05:45,630 --> 00:05:47,630
and he's been taking warfarin ever since.

122
00:05:47,630 --> 00:05:49,430
His D-dimer is normal this time,

123
00:05:49,480 --> 00:05:50,720
but he's had a persistent

124
00:05:50,720 --> 00:05:52,000
fever and cough.

125
00:05:52,720 --> 00:05:55,830
The X-rays look like an infection
no matter how you look at them.

126
00:05:55,830 --> 00:05:56,750
How strange.

127
00:05:58,680 --> 00:06:00,360
Could it be tuberculosis?

128
00:06:01,000 --> 00:06:02,870
I suspected TB at first, too.

129
00:06:02,870 --> 00:06:03,510
But

130
00:06:03,510 --> 00:06:05,160
we did a TB smear

131
00:06:05,160 --> 00:06:06,430
and TB antibody test
when he was admitted,

132
00:06:06,430 --> 00:06:07,510
and both came back negative.

133
00:06:07,510 --> 00:06:09,040
We have no evidence
to support that diagnosis.

134
00:06:09,040 --> 00:06:11,070
If we can't figure out what's causing it,

135
00:06:11,070 --> 00:06:12,600
maybe we should persuade him

136
00:06:12,600 --> 00:06:13,270
to transfer to another hospital.

137
00:06:13,270 --> 00:06:15,400
We can't let this delay his treatment.

138
00:06:15,870 --> 00:06:17,670
I suggested that from the start,

139
00:06:18,120 --> 00:06:20,000
but they don't want the hassle.

140
00:06:20,310 --> 00:06:21,390
Their family's not well-off.

141
00:06:21,390 --> 00:06:25,320
Coming to our Xiaoximen Hospital
is already stretching their budget.

142
00:06:25,870 --> 00:06:27,530
If only Zhengliang were here.

143
00:06:28,680 --> 00:06:30,740
How would it be better if he were here?

144
00:06:30,920 --> 00:06:32,050
Am I not good enough?

145
00:06:32,360 --> 00:06:33,960
Can't you discuss it with me?

146
00:06:34,390 --> 00:06:35,720
Even if I discuss it with you,
can you solve it?

147
00:06:35,720 --> 00:06:37,070
Why can't I?

148
00:06:39,680 --> 00:06:41,270
Of course I can.

149
00:06:42,430 --> 00:06:43,720
Didn't you just say

150
00:06:43,720 --> 00:06:44,830
you suspected TB?

151
00:06:44,870 --> 00:06:46,870
You have to trust your own judgment.

152
00:06:47,430 --> 00:06:49,310
What's the point of me trusting myself?

153
00:06:49,310 --> 00:06:50,790
This is a matter of life and death.

154
00:06:50,790 --> 00:06:52,190
I can't just go with my gut.

155
00:06:52,190 --> 00:06:53,790
I need scientific evidence.

156
00:06:54,190 --> 00:06:55,190
It's okay.

157
00:06:55,240 --> 00:06:57,920
T-There will always be a way.

158
00:06:58,510 --> 00:06:59,390
Don't worry.

159
00:07:01,390 --> 00:07:02,480
Alright, you go eat.

160
00:07:02,480 --> 00:07:03,810
I'll take another look.

161
00:07:17,240 --> 00:07:18,360
But from the smear

162
00:07:18,360 --> 00:07:19,360
and the antibody test...

163
00:07:18,920 --> 00:07:21,830
[Quiet]

164
00:07:19,360 --> 00:07:20,960
Let's put those aside for now

165
00:07:21,000 --> 00:07:22,560
and think about what President
always says:

166
00:07:22,560 --> 00:07:24,310
look at the patient as a whole.

167
00:07:24,310 --> 00:07:25,560
The patient's elderly,

168
00:07:25,560 --> 00:07:27,040
his family isn't well-off,

169
00:07:27,040 --> 00:07:28,240
he drinks heavily,

170
00:07:28,950 --> 00:07:30,390
and he's visibly emaciated

171
00:07:30,390 --> 00:07:31,560
and malnourished.

172
00:07:31,950 --> 00:07:33,080
He's had a prolonged

173
00:07:33,110 --> 00:07:34,000
fever and cough,

174
00:07:34,000 --> 00:07:35,750
and antibiotics haven't worked.

175
00:07:35,750 --> 00:07:36,750
All these factors

176
00:07:36,750 --> 00:07:38,159
point to TB.

177
00:07:38,360 --> 00:07:39,190
Plus,

178
00:07:39,240 --> 00:07:40,870
the positive rate
for tubercle bacillus smears

179
00:07:40,870 --> 00:07:41,390
is relatively low.

180
00:07:41,390 --> 00:07:43,260
Just because the first test was negative

181
00:07:43,260 --> 00:07:45,000
doesn't necessarily rule out TB.

182
00:07:45,000 --> 00:07:47,000
Aren't you being a bit argumentative?

183
00:07:47,000 --> 00:07:47,390
Wait,

184
00:07:47,390 --> 00:07:49,120
how is that being argumentative?

185
00:07:49,120 --> 00:07:50,500
You just don't trust my judgment,

186
00:07:50,500 --> 00:07:51,040
do you?

187
00:07:51,040 --> 00:07:54,510
-If Liu Zhengliang were here…
-It wouldn't matter who was here!

188
00:07:54,510 --> 00:07:56,310
The scans are right there.

189
00:07:56,480 --> 00:07:58,409
This patient simply can't have TB.

190
00:07:59,310 --> 00:08:00,810
Medically speaking, there's no such thing

191
00:08:00,810 --> 00:08:02,670
as a 100% definitive conclusion.

192
00:08:02,680 --> 00:08:04,880
You can't just rule out the possibility

193
00:08:05,160 --> 00:08:06,160
Dr. Che mentioned.

194
00:08:06,160 --> 00:08:07,310
Chen Junnan.

195
00:08:09,310 --> 00:08:10,750
Can you stop making things
more complicated?

196
00:08:10,750 --> 00:08:12,600
How am I making things more complicated?

197
00:08:12,600 --> 00:08:14,360
We have no other leads, do we?

198
00:08:15,000 --> 00:08:16,920
Then why not try

199
00:08:17,070 --> 00:08:17,950
Dr. Che's approach?

200
00:08:17,950 --> 00:08:19,550
How are we supposed to try it?

201
00:08:19,680 --> 00:08:22,630
Doctors have to take responsibility
for what they say.

202
00:08:22,630 --> 00:08:24,430
This isn't like shopping for clothes,

203
00:08:24,430 --> 00:08:25,510
where you can just try something on
at random, okay?

204
00:08:25,510 --> 00:08:27,160
How is that irresponsible?

205
00:08:27,190 --> 00:08:29,120
And how is it just trying something
at random?

206
00:08:29,120 --> 00:08:30,120
Dr. Che has a reasoned hypothesis,

207
00:08:30,120 --> 00:08:31,630
doesn't she?

208
00:08:31,630 --> 00:08:32,150
Junnan...

209
00:08:32,150 --> 00:08:33,360
Don't interrupt.

210
00:08:33,630 --> 00:08:34,440
Jin.

211
00:08:33,850 --> 00:08:40,600
[ICU]

212
00:08:36,870 --> 00:08:37,909
Did we collect a sputum sample
from the patient

213
00:08:37,909 --> 00:08:39,770
before he was admitted to the ICU?

214
00:08:39,960 --> 00:08:40,789
Yes, once.

215
00:08:40,789 --> 00:08:41,850
Once isn't enough.

216
00:08:43,750 --> 00:08:44,750
We need 3 samples

217
00:08:44,960 --> 00:08:46,440
to ensure an adequate concentration,

218
00:08:46,440 --> 00:08:48,080
so we can test them for

219
00:08:48,080 --> 00:08:49,200
TB DNA.

220
00:08:49,320 --> 00:08:50,150
But

221
00:08:50,150 --> 00:08:52,010
our hospital can't run that test.

222
00:08:52,910 --> 00:08:54,440
I'll contact No. 1 Hospital

223
00:08:55,150 --> 00:08:56,600
and take the samples there myself.

224
00:08:56,600 --> 00:08:58,360
But our whole department is swamped.

225
00:08:58,360 --> 00:08:58,840
Who's going to take them?

226
00:08:58,840 --> 00:09:00,600
I will. I'll drive them over.

227
00:09:00,670 --> 00:09:01,630
And one test won't be enough—

228
00:09:01,630 --> 00:09:02,550
we need 3.

229
00:09:02,570 --> 00:09:04,120
We can't draw any conclusions

230
00:09:04,120 --> 00:09:05,120
until we get all 3 results.

231
00:09:05,120 --> 00:09:05,720
Come on...

232
00:09:05,720 --> 00:09:07,520
Don't you think that's a hassle?

233
00:09:08,110 --> 00:09:09,770
I've got nothing better to do.

234
00:09:10,270 --> 00:09:12,440
I'm the perfect person for the job.

235
00:09:20,890 --> 00:09:23,650
[Dream Garden Themed Hotel]

236
00:09:23,600 --> 00:09:26,260
There are so many
small appliance repair shops.

237
00:09:29,000 --> 00:09:30,480
So this is the so-called

238
00:09:30,510 --> 00:09:31,670
"love hotel"?

239
00:09:33,000 --> 00:09:33,910
You bet.

240
00:09:35,000 --> 00:09:35,790
This place

241
00:09:36,030 --> 00:09:37,240
used to be an ordinary

242
00:09:37,510 --> 00:09:39,260
little in.

243
00:09:39,440 --> 00:09:41,040
It was renovated 3 years ago.

244
00:09:41,390 --> 00:09:42,270
Some idiot designer

245
00:09:42,270 --> 00:09:43,840
came out of nowhere

246
00:09:43,960 --> 00:09:46,200
and claimed this kind of decor
would bring in more business.

247
00:09:46,200 --> 00:09:47,530
That woman believed him

248
00:09:47,960 --> 00:09:49,240
and poured a ton of money into it.

249
00:09:49,240 --> 00:09:50,720
But after the renovation,

250
00:09:50,750 --> 00:09:52,030
business was even worse than before.

251
00:09:52,030 --> 00:09:53,030
That woman?

252
00:09:54,120 --> 00:09:55,050
He means his mom.

253
00:09:58,510 --> 00:10:00,840
That the... the what?

254
00:10:04,440 --> 00:10:06,170
What does it have to do with you?

255
00:10:06,600 --> 00:10:07,840
Dream theme.

256
00:10:08,240 --> 00:10:09,370
Oh, so it's "theme".

257
00:10:12,240 --> 00:10:13,390
But wouldn't it be a bit weird for me

258
00:10:13,390 --> 00:10:14,790
to be staying here alone?

259
00:10:15,000 --> 00:10:15,750
Yeah.

260
00:10:15,750 --> 00:10:17,440
It's pretty weird and inappropriate.

261
00:10:17,440 --> 00:10:18,750
Why don't you find somewhere else?

262
00:10:18,750 --> 00:10:19,670
No way.

263
00:10:20,390 --> 00:10:21,840
Aren't you staying here alone too?

264
00:10:21,840 --> 00:10:22,240
What,

265
00:10:22,240 --> 00:10:23,840
you can stay here but I can't?

266
00:10:24,080 --> 00:10:25,510
I'm staying here because it's cheap.

267
00:10:25,510 --> 00:10:26,440
30 yuan a day.

268
00:10:26,440 --> 00:10:27,080
You won't find a deal like that
anywhere else.

269
00:10:27,080 --> 00:10:27,940
I'm broke, too.

270
00:10:27,960 --> 00:10:28,870
I want a cheap place, too.

271
00:10:28,870 --> 00:10:29,600
Sis.

272
00:10:31,510 --> 00:10:32,970
For you, it's 20 yuan a day,

273
00:10:33,120 --> 00:10:34,510
and you get a free bottle of soy milk.

274
00:10:34,510 --> 00:10:35,630
You are so nice.

275
00:10:35,630 --> 00:10:37,760
No need. Just charge me the same as him.

276
00:10:38,550 --> 00:10:39,390
Give me that

277
00:10:39,390 --> 00:10:41,630
t-theme thing.

278
00:10:41,630 --> 00:10:42,790
D-D-Dream.

279
00:10:43,200 --> 00:10:44,400
Let me experience it.

280
00:10:53,150 --> 00:10:54,080
Look at Pink.

281
00:10:54,080 --> 00:10:56,910
The second he heard he had to
carry the suitcase, he took off.

282
00:10:56,910 --> 00:10:58,030
So you do realize

283
00:10:58,030 --> 00:10:59,550
this suitcase is freaking heavy, huh?

284
00:10:59,550 --> 00:11:01,510
How do you think I hauled it
all the way here?

285
00:11:01,510 --> 00:11:02,440
It's your own suitcase.

286
00:11:02,440 --> 00:11:03,870
Why should someone else carry it for you?

287
00:11:03,870 --> 00:11:05,550
I never asked him to carry it for me.

288
00:11:04,530 --> 00:11:06,090
[Friendly Reminder: Surveillance Cameras in Use—
Please Be Mindful of Your Words and Actions]

289
00:11:07,390 --> 00:11:08,200
Hold on.

290
00:11:10,030 --> 00:11:11,430
Let's get this straight.

291
00:11:12,240 --> 00:11:13,440
When are you leaving?

292
00:11:21,550 --> 00:11:22,550
What do you want?

293
00:11:26,750 --> 00:11:28,510
That depends on when you leave.

294
00:11:28,510 --> 00:11:29,770
I leave when you leave.

295
00:11:30,670 --> 00:11:31,870
Stop messing around.

296
00:11:32,390 --> 00:11:33,270
What if I stay here

297
00:11:33,270 --> 00:11:34,530
for the rest of my life?

298
00:11:35,390 --> 00:11:36,720
Like you really mean it.

299
00:11:36,960 --> 00:11:39,630
It snows here in winter too.

300
00:11:43,550 --> 00:11:45,670
Didn't you have something to say to me?

301
00:11:45,670 --> 00:11:46,480
Say it now.

302
00:11:59,390 --> 00:12:00,320
So...

303
00:12:01,600 --> 00:12:02,670
After I finish,

304
00:12:03,270 --> 00:12:05,070
you'll just send me away, right?

305
00:12:08,630 --> 00:12:10,080
How dare you nod?

306
00:12:11,510 --> 00:12:12,550
I'll tell you

307
00:12:12,670 --> 00:12:13,720
when I leave.

308
00:12:16,630 --> 00:12:18,030
Are you coming in with me?

309
00:12:28,550 --> 00:12:29,680
Wait, what's wrong?

310
00:12:34,870 --> 00:12:35,870
See if you sink in.

311
00:12:38,270 --> 00:12:39,550
I'm already sinking!

312
00:12:39,720 --> 00:12:41,240
Why is it so wobbly?

313
00:12:41,600 --> 00:12:43,440
It feels like...

314
00:12:43,750 --> 00:12:45,750
Like I've had my spine pulled out.

315
00:12:46,270 --> 00:12:47,600
Is that why you yelled?

316
00:12:48,510 --> 00:12:50,510
H-Have you ever slept on a waterbed?

317
00:12:50,750 --> 00:12:51,480
No.

318
00:12:51,480 --> 00:12:52,650
There you go, then.

319
00:12:54,320 --> 00:12:56,120
T-This is so wild.

320
00:12:56,120 --> 00:12:57,250
Sleeping in this...

321
00:12:58,320 --> 00:12:59,150
What's the theme of this room again?

322
00:12:59,150 --> 00:13:00,440
The Caribbean?

323
00:13:01,080 --> 00:13:02,680
Why do you insist on staying?

324
00:13:11,200 --> 00:13:12,000
You...

325
00:13:12,360 --> 00:13:14,690
Why are you in such a hurry
to make me leave?

326
00:13:19,120 --> 00:13:19,870
I'm scared.

327
00:13:23,120 --> 00:13:23,870
Scared of me?

328
00:13:24,910 --> 00:13:25,720
Yes.

329
00:13:26,390 --> 00:13:27,200
Of you.

330
00:13:28,910 --> 00:13:29,970
And of myself, too.

331
00:13:52,480 --> 00:13:53,200
When I came here,

332
00:13:53,200 --> 00:13:54,730
I'd already made up my mind.

333
00:13:59,720 --> 00:14:01,480
I'm not here for a fling.

334
00:14:05,870 --> 00:14:07,070
I want to take you home

335
00:14:10,910 --> 00:14:12,200
and build a relationship with you,

336
00:14:12,200 --> 00:14:13,200
one with a future,

337
00:14:14,200 --> 00:14:15,270
a journey,

338
00:14:19,270 --> 00:14:21,120
and a happy ending.

339
00:14:21,510 --> 00:14:22,600
I can't go back.

340
00:14:22,840 --> 00:14:24,510
B-But why?

341
00:14:25,030 --> 00:14:26,960
What do you mean, you can't go back?

342
00:14:28,150 --> 00:14:29,790
There are plenty of illnesses in the world
that can't be cured,

343
00:14:29,790 --> 00:14:31,000
but yours isn't one of them.

344
00:14:31,000 --> 00:14:32,630
It is. I'm a doctor.

345
00:14:32,630 --> 00:14:34,360
Like doctors know everything.

346
00:14:35,150 --> 00:14:36,610
So what if you're a doctor?

347
00:14:36,750 --> 00:14:38,750
"One cannot save oneself,
nor can a doctor heal himself."

348
00:14:38,750 --> 00:14:39,550
You know that?

349
00:14:39,840 --> 00:14:41,200
Even audiobooks say so.

350
00:14:42,840 --> 00:14:43,630
What?

351
00:14:49,000 --> 00:14:50,200
You two are busy, huh?

352
00:14:53,550 --> 00:14:55,320
Well, I saw the door was open,

353
00:14:55,320 --> 00:14:57,480
so I wanted to ask if you need anything.

354
00:14:58,750 --> 00:14:59,840
I-I'll come back later.

355
00:14:59,840 --> 00:15:01,040
Cut it out. Come back.

356
00:15:02,240 --> 00:15:03,300
What's wrong, Sis?

357
00:15:04,030 --> 00:15:05,870
We're both dressed properly.

358
00:15:06,030 --> 00:15:07,320
What can't you talk to us?

359
00:15:07,320 --> 00:15:08,110
What is it?

360
00:15:09,720 --> 00:15:10,480
Well,

361
00:15:11,360 --> 00:15:12,150
sis,

362
00:15:13,320 --> 00:15:14,150
do you have any plans

363
00:15:14,150 --> 00:15:15,360
for the next few days?

364
00:15:18,910 --> 00:15:20,000
Not for now.

365
00:15:21,150 --> 00:15:22,150
Here's the thing.

366
00:15:23,240 --> 00:15:24,320
You see,

367
00:15:24,480 --> 00:15:26,080
Zhengliang promised

368
00:15:26,360 --> 00:15:27,750
to hang out with me for a few days.

369
00:15:27,750 --> 00:15:29,280
When did I promise you that?

370
00:15:30,320 --> 00:15:31,120
Move.

371
00:15:33,240 --> 00:15:34,030
But...

372
00:15:36,790 --> 00:15:38,000
We agreed on that

373
00:15:38,000 --> 00:15:39,530
when we discussed the rent,

374
00:15:41,120 --> 00:15:41,790
didn't we?

375
00:15:41,790 --> 00:15:43,020
That I... I...

376
00:15:43,120 --> 00:15:44,240
I'd give you a discount,

377
00:15:44,240 --> 00:15:45,700
and you'd hang out with me.

378
00:15:45,750 --> 00:15:46,910
I even helped you submit

379
00:15:46,910 --> 00:15:47,870
your resume.

380
00:15:48,030 --> 00:15:49,720
Pink! Pink!

381
00:15:53,030 --> 00:15:53,720
Look at him.

382
00:15:53,720 --> 00:15:54,360
What did he

383
00:15:55,360 --> 00:15:56,720
promise to do with you?

384
00:15:57,200 --> 00:15:58,200
Count me in.

385
00:15:59,320 --> 00:16:01,550
That's exactly what I meant.

386
00:16:01,750 --> 00:16:02,550
Right?

387
00:16:03,150 --> 00:16:03,960
Well,

388
00:16:04,150 --> 00:16:06,150
Sis, you just got here.

389
00:16:06,510 --> 00:16:07,320
Is there anywhere

390
00:16:07,320 --> 00:16:08,510
you'd like to go?

391
00:16:09,000 --> 00:16:10,120
I don't know anyone or anything
around here.

392
00:16:10,120 --> 00:16:11,520
How am I supposed to know?

393
00:16:15,670 --> 00:16:16,480
Perfect.

394
00:16:17,270 --> 00:16:18,480
I know

395
00:16:18,670 --> 00:16:19,870
just the place.

396
00:16:20,910 --> 00:16:22,570
I promise you'll have a blast.

397
00:16:23,550 --> 00:16:24,680
It'll be really fun.

398
00:16:33,030 --> 00:16:33,960
You wait there for the results.

399
00:16:33,960 --> 00:16:34,910
I'll head back to the ICU
and wait for the samples.

400
00:16:34,910 --> 00:16:37,570
Don't worry.
I'll get them to you as soon as I can.

401
00:16:40,670 --> 00:16:41,470
[For Laboratory Testing Only]

402
00:16:51,750 --> 00:16:52,670
Don't worry.

403
00:16:52,840 --> 00:16:54,270
It's normal not to get it
on the first try.

404
00:16:54,270 --> 00:16:56,000
You don't need to tell me. Go on.

405
00:17:19,109 --> 00:17:19,920
How is it?

406
00:17:20,720 --> 00:17:21,680
Guess what?

407
00:17:21,920 --> 00:17:22,750
Let me see.

408
00:17:23,680 --> 00:17:24,670
Guess first.

409
00:17:29,000 --> 00:17:29,880
They found it.

410
00:17:30,950 --> 00:17:32,000
It's TB.

411
00:17:33,070 --> 00:17:34,730
The cause has been confirmed!

412
00:17:35,920 --> 00:17:36,640
You won.

413
00:17:37,400 --> 00:17:38,630
We won.

414
00:17:41,920 --> 00:17:42,720
Thank you.

415
00:17:52,640 --> 00:17:52,920
Dr. Jin.

416
00:17:52,920 --> 00:17:53,550
The new patient's

417
00:17:53,550 --> 00:17:54,680
test results are in.

418
00:17:54,830 --> 00:17:55,760
It's confirmed.

419
00:17:56,350 --> 00:17:57,400
It's TB.

420
00:17:57,960 --> 00:17:58,750
We can now transfer the patient

421
00:17:58,750 --> 00:18:00,310
to a negative-pressure isolation room,

422
00:18:00,310 --> 00:18:01,790
call the infectious disease hospital
for a consultation,

423
00:18:01,790 --> 00:18:04,520
and start anti-TB treatment
as soon as possible.

424
00:18:05,100 --> 00:18:06,020
That's great!

425
00:18:06,830 --> 00:18:08,270
He really came through.

426
00:18:08,400 --> 00:18:09,240
Can you tell what Li

427
00:18:09,240 --> 00:18:10,750
and Jin have written

428
00:18:10,750 --> 00:18:11,960
in their eyes?

429
00:18:12,480 --> 00:18:13,240
What?

430
00:18:13,480 --> 00:18:14,480
"Respect!"

431
00:18:15,000 --> 00:18:16,310
In big, bold letters!

432
00:18:17,110 --> 00:18:18,960
We make a great team, don't we?

433
00:18:19,720 --> 00:18:22,110
If it weren't for your sharp diagnosis

434
00:18:23,030 --> 00:18:24,720
and my quick reflexes,

435
00:18:23,730 --> 00:18:27,080
[To the Ob-GYN ward]
[To the Operating Room]

436
00:18:25,200 --> 00:18:26,860
we'd have delayed treatment.

437
00:18:27,200 --> 00:18:29,550
Just think how much
the patient would've suffered.

438
00:18:29,550 --> 00:18:31,400
Come on, admit it.

439
00:18:32,110 --> 00:18:33,510
I'm pretty much

440
00:18:34,030 --> 00:18:35,160
on Liu Zhengliang's level now,

441
00:18:35,160 --> 00:18:36,720
aren't I?

442
00:18:39,000 --> 00:18:40,720
Not quite.

443
00:18:41,240 --> 00:18:43,570
You two aren't even in the same dimension.

444
00:18:43,640 --> 00:18:45,200
What do you mean,
not in the same dimension?

445
00:18:45,200 --> 00:18:45,960
What,

446
00:18:47,240 --> 00:18:50,350
is he in the first dimension
and I'm in the second or something?

447
00:18:50,350 --> 00:18:52,150
Come on, give me a little praise.

448
00:18:52,880 --> 00:18:54,000
Just a little.

449
00:19:22,720 --> 00:19:23,510
Lyu.

450
00:19:24,000 --> 00:19:24,960
What's going on?

451
00:19:26,440 --> 00:19:27,240
It's nothing.

452
00:19:28,000 --> 00:19:31,400
The NHC is conducting a joint audit
with the tax authorities.

453
00:20:31,920 --> 00:20:33,680
Come on, bread, bread.

454
00:20:34,750 --> 00:20:36,750
Bread, bread. Come on, bread.

455
00:20:37,960 --> 00:20:38,960
Help yourselves.

456
00:20:42,070 --> 00:20:43,240
Come on.

457
00:20:43,880 --> 00:20:44,880
Help yourselves.

458
00:20:45,790 --> 00:20:46,450
Here you go.

459
00:20:46,880 --> 00:20:47,830
Help yourselves.

460
00:20:47,830 --> 00:20:48,750
Come on.

461
00:20:49,510 --> 00:20:50,480
There's enough for everyone.

462
00:20:50,480 --> 00:20:51,830
Ask me if it's not enough.

463
00:20:51,830 --> 00:20:52,480
Come on.

464
00:20:52,830 --> 00:20:53,750
No, thanks.

465
00:20:53,750 --> 00:20:54,550
My hands are too dirty.

466
00:20:54,550 --> 00:20:55,880
Are there any wet wipes?

467
00:20:55,880 --> 00:20:57,240
Good job, everyone.

468
00:20:57,270 --> 00:20:57,880
You're not eating?

469
00:20:57,880 --> 00:20:58,340
I'm not.

470
00:20:58,350 --> 00:20:59,440
I'm so tired.

471
00:20:59,790 --> 00:21:01,320
Being an extra is so tiring.

472
00:21:01,510 --> 00:21:04,270
I think being an extra is fun.

473
00:21:05,310 --> 00:21:06,200
What's fun about it?

474
00:21:06,200 --> 00:21:07,400
Look at this steep slope.

475
00:21:07,400 --> 00:21:09,130
How many times have we run up it?

476
00:21:09,750 --> 00:21:10,550
We made

477
00:21:12,160 --> 00:21:13,490
12 round trips, I think.

478
00:21:15,200 --> 00:21:15,960
Shooting scenes like this

479
00:21:15,960 --> 00:21:17,290
must use up a lot of film.

480
00:21:19,160 --> 00:21:19,750
No, Sis.

481
00:21:21,200 --> 00:21:22,960
It's all digital cameras now.

482
00:21:23,110 --> 00:21:24,480
They don't use film anymore.

483
00:21:24,480 --> 00:21:25,610
You know quite a lot.

484
00:21:28,270 --> 00:21:29,670
I've done some research.

485
00:21:30,110 --> 00:21:31,030
I have...

486
00:21:33,550 --> 00:21:35,750
I've always wanted to experience

487
00:21:35,830 --> 00:21:37,430
what it's like to be an extra,

488
00:21:38,790 --> 00:21:40,520
and today I finally got to do it.

489
00:21:41,400 --> 00:21:42,200
What a blast!

490
00:21:44,440 --> 00:21:45,680
You had your blast.

491
00:21:45,680 --> 00:21:46,960
But my legs are about to cramp.

492
00:21:46,960 --> 00:21:48,690
I'm almost half dead, you know?

493
00:21:51,000 --> 00:21:51,590
I mean,

494
00:21:52,240 --> 00:21:53,790
this is all the production crew
gave us to drink?

495
00:21:53,790 --> 00:21:55,000
It's freezing cold.

496
00:21:56,200 --> 00:21:57,800
Does this crew not have that?

497
00:21:58,440 --> 00:21:59,960
Don't stars usually treat people

498
00:21:59,960 --> 00:22:01,790
to bubble tea or something?

499
00:22:01,830 --> 00:22:03,230
Don't the extras get any?

500
00:22:03,960 --> 00:22:05,310
You should be grateful we got this, Sis.

501
00:22:05,310 --> 00:22:06,000
Is that so?

502
00:22:07,070 --> 00:22:08,000
Hey, beautiful!

503
00:22:09,440 --> 00:22:09,960
Me?

504
00:22:09,960 --> 00:22:10,510
A-Are you talking to me?

505
00:22:10,510 --> 00:22:11,480
Yes, you.

506
00:22:11,880 --> 00:22:12,240
We've got a role

507
00:22:12,240 --> 00:22:13,480
for a battlefield nurse here.

508
00:22:13,480 --> 00:22:14,340
Can you play it?

509
00:22:16,750 --> 00:22:17,640
Look at that.

510
00:22:17,920 --> 00:22:19,070
I'm a natural beauty.

511
00:22:19,070 --> 00:22:20,200
Even with makeup like this,

512
00:22:20,200 --> 00:22:21,640
I can't hide my good looks.

513
00:22:21,640 --> 00:22:23,200
You're the only woman here.

514
00:22:24,000 --> 00:22:25,400
You deserve the cramps.

515
00:22:26,920 --> 00:22:27,920
No, thanks, man.

516
00:22:27,920 --> 00:22:29,920
Let me cool off a bit. I'm exhausted.

517
00:22:30,070 --> 00:22:31,330
I'm sweating baskets.

518
00:22:31,510 --> 00:22:32,830
It's "sweating buckets."

519
00:22:32,830 --> 00:22:34,720
Beautiful, this role has lines.

520
00:22:34,720 --> 00:22:35,780
I'll pay you extra.

521
00:22:37,110 --> 00:22:37,790
Sis.

522
00:22:40,110 --> 00:22:41,000
It's a great opportunity.

523
00:22:41,000 --> 00:22:41,640
What do you mean?

524
00:22:41,640 --> 00:22:42,840
You've got to take it.

525
00:22:43,550 --> 00:22:44,920
Will it cover 3 bubble teas?

526
00:22:44,920 --> 00:22:46,500
It'll cover at least 6.

527
00:22:48,270 --> 00:22:49,070
Wait for me.

528
00:22:49,550 --> 00:22:51,110
-Come on! I'll do it!
-Alright! Come on.

529
00:22:51,110 --> 00:22:52,030
Be careful.

530
00:22:53,440 --> 00:22:54,070
Buddy.

531
00:22:54,200 --> 00:22:55,680
Can you give me a little hint
about the scene?

532
00:22:55,680 --> 00:22:57,960
I'm pretty good at
crying scenes and stuff.

533
00:22:57,960 --> 00:22:59,480
Your character is all about excitement,

534
00:22:59,480 --> 00:22:59,880
-passion, and...
-Excitement?

535
00:22:59,880 --> 00:23:00,960
Right, and killing enemies.

536
00:23:00,960 --> 00:23:03,160
So I just scream my head off like before?

537
00:23:03,440 --> 00:23:04,240
Director.

538
00:23:04,750 --> 00:23:06,350
What do you think of her?

539
00:23:07,790 --> 00:23:10,240
This makeup might make it hard to see
what I really look like.

540
00:23:10,240 --> 00:23:11,570
She's decent-looking.

541
00:23:11,790 --> 00:23:12,550
Alright, let's go with her.

542
00:23:12,550 --> 00:23:13,350
Hurry up and get changed.

543
00:23:13,350 --> 00:23:14,480
Okay, got it.

544
00:23:15,110 --> 00:23:17,030
What do you mean "decent-looking"?

545
00:23:17,030 --> 00:23:18,270
Alright, wardrobe and makeup.

546
00:23:18,270 --> 00:23:18,720
Come over here.

547
00:23:18,720 --> 00:23:19,790
Clean her face up

548
00:23:19,790 --> 00:23:21,240
and get her changed.

549
00:23:21,240 --> 00:23:22,000
Here.

550
00:23:22,350 --> 00:23:23,920
These are Nurse Qian's lines.

551
00:23:23,920 --> 00:23:25,050
Read them carefully

552
00:23:25,200 --> 00:23:25,750
and memorize them.

553
00:23:25,750 --> 00:23:27,880
I'll run through them with you in a bit.

554
00:23:28,680 --> 00:23:30,480
Soldiers over there, come here.

555
00:23:37,550 --> 00:23:41,160
[Monitor]

556
00:23:53,190 --> 00:23:58,460
[Monitor]

557
00:23:56,480 --> 00:23:58,010
How's it going, beautiful?

558
00:23:58,640 --> 00:23:59,920
Here, I'll run through them with you.

559
00:23:59,920 --> 00:24:02,030
Buddy, you...

560
00:24:02,030 --> 00:24:02,830
Could you

561
00:24:02,960 --> 00:24:03,830
run through it for me first?

562
00:24:03,830 --> 00:24:04,960
Or is there

563
00:24:04,960 --> 00:24:06,000
an audio version of the script?

564
00:24:06,000 --> 00:24:07,110
Maybe you can talk to the director.

565
00:24:07,110 --> 00:24:08,310
Audio version?

566
00:24:08,510 --> 00:24:09,920
Wait, you can't read?

567
00:24:10,270 --> 00:24:12,390
[Monitor]

568
00:24:10,880 --> 00:24:11,880
Um, well...

569
00:24:11,880 --> 00:24:12,550
Um,

570
00:24:12,920 --> 00:24:13,720
I'm sorry.

571
00:24:13,830 --> 00:24:14,750
We're in a hurry,

572
00:24:14,750 --> 00:24:15,590
so she's out.

573
00:24:15,640 --> 00:24:17,550
Go on, change into your own clothes.

574
00:24:17,550 --> 00:24:19,030
But we had a deal!

575
00:24:17,800 --> 00:24:20,890
[Monitor]

576
00:24:19,030 --> 00:24:19,690
You guys...

577
00:24:36,270 --> 00:24:37,750
You were so cool today.

578
00:24:37,920 --> 00:24:39,550
Seriously. Such a real man.

579
00:24:39,830 --> 00:24:41,030
So tough and badass.

580
00:24:41,480 --> 00:24:43,880
I just didn't want you
to embarrass yourself.

581
00:24:43,880 --> 00:24:46,240
If you're not cut out for the job,
don't force it.

582
00:24:46,240 --> 00:24:47,160
Who said I wanted this gig?

583
00:24:47,160 --> 00:24:49,220
He's the one who wanted it, remember?

584
00:24:51,200 --> 00:24:52,350
Anyway,

585
00:24:52,590 --> 00:24:54,050
I appreciate what you did.

586
00:24:57,400 --> 00:24:58,860
It's just that sometimes,

587
00:24:59,240 --> 00:25:01,350
I forget that I'm sick.

588
00:25:02,240 --> 00:25:03,640
I'm sure you understand.

589
00:25:05,590 --> 00:25:06,440
But then

590
00:25:08,400 --> 00:25:10,860
life has a way of reminding you
out of nowhere

591
00:25:11,480 --> 00:25:13,680
that you two aren't like everyone else.

592
00:25:13,720 --> 00:25:14,790
You two are sick.

593
00:25:20,790 --> 00:25:21,720
You two are sick?

594
00:25:23,510 --> 00:25:24,640
Yeah. Minor issues.

595
00:25:25,440 --> 00:25:26,920
If you're sick, you need to get treated.

596
00:25:26,920 --> 00:25:27,720
Right?

597
00:25:28,310 --> 00:25:29,110
See?

598
00:25:29,510 --> 00:25:30,550
Even your buddy here knows

599
00:25:30,550 --> 00:25:32,150
sick people need treatment.

600
00:25:32,510 --> 00:25:33,680
Mine's terminal.

601
00:25:33,880 --> 00:25:34,830
There's no cure.

602
00:25:36,880 --> 00:25:38,550
You also have a terminal illness, bro?

603
00:25:38,550 --> 00:25:39,590
What's it to you?

604
00:25:39,590 --> 00:25:41,190
And what do you mean, "also"?

605
00:25:42,550 --> 00:25:44,200
I was just asking.

606
00:25:44,590 --> 00:25:45,790
Poor choice of words.

607
00:25:58,480 --> 00:25:59,310
Give me one.

608
00:26:02,750 --> 00:26:03,680
Unfortunately,

609
00:26:03,720 --> 00:26:05,050
it's the last one again.

610
00:26:05,240 --> 00:26:06,550
What are the odds?

611
00:26:07,070 --> 00:26:08,470
Let me see your candy tin.

612
00:26:10,750 --> 00:26:11,000
Well, bro,

613
00:26:11,000 --> 00:26:12,440
what's there to see?

614
00:26:12,440 --> 00:26:13,440
What's the harm?

615
00:26:13,440 --> 00:26:14,510
Your buddy wants to see it, so let him.

616
00:26:14,510 --> 00:26:15,480
Come on. What's the big deal?

617
00:26:15,480 --> 00:26:16,480
Quit stalling.

618
00:26:17,240 --> 00:26:18,720
Hey, why are you so stingy?

619
00:26:18,720 --> 00:26:20,180
There are still some left,

620
00:26:20,240 --> 00:26:21,970
yet you told me there were none.

621
00:26:25,240 --> 00:26:27,200
This isn't candy. It's medicine.

622
00:26:29,070 --> 00:26:29,830
Medicine?

623
00:26:30,960 --> 00:26:32,000
Are you sick?

624
00:26:33,310 --> 00:26:34,590
What kind of medicine is this?

625
00:26:34,590 --> 00:26:36,320
Why put medicine in a candy tin?

626
00:26:38,640 --> 00:26:39,840
Just a minor illness.

627
00:26:40,510 --> 00:26:41,640
I just thought

628
00:26:42,270 --> 00:26:43,550
pill bottles were ugly,

629
00:26:43,550 --> 00:26:44,510
and this tin

630
00:26:44,510 --> 00:26:45,640
suits me better.

631
00:26:46,350 --> 00:26:47,240
Besides,

632
00:26:47,590 --> 00:26:49,400
it's not some controlled substance.

633
00:26:49,400 --> 00:26:50,460
Just painkillers.

634
00:26:53,310 --> 00:26:54,000
Zhou Zheng.

635
00:26:54,200 --> 00:26:55,000
Tell me the truth.

636
00:26:55,000 --> 00:26:56,310
What's your condition?

637
00:26:56,310 --> 00:26:58,240
Come on, tell him.

638
00:26:58,270 --> 00:26:59,590
He's an amazing doctor.

639
00:26:59,590 --> 00:27:00,790
He can cure anything.

640
00:27:00,830 --> 00:27:01,590
Don't exaggerate.

641
00:27:01,590 --> 00:27:03,030
I can't even cure myself.

642
00:27:04,310 --> 00:27:05,110
What is it?

643
00:27:11,880 --> 00:27:13,030
Glioblastoma.

644
00:27:13,110 --> 00:27:13,920
What?

645
00:27:14,110 --> 00:27:15,000
Say that again!

646
00:27:22,640 --> 00:27:23,960
Glioblastoma.

647
00:27:25,510 --> 00:27:26,240
See?

648
00:27:26,790 --> 00:27:28,830
I told you I'm the chosen one.

649
00:27:30,270 --> 00:27:31,200
Awesome, right?

650
00:27:42,350 --> 00:27:43,880
W-What kind of tumor?

651
00:27:43,880 --> 00:27:45,830
Is it serious?

652
00:27:46,790 --> 00:27:49,450
When we get back,
let me take a look at your scans.

653
00:28:03,710 --> 00:28:08,930
[Dream Garden Themed Hotel]

654
00:28:14,790 --> 00:28:16,790
Could it be a misdiagnosis?

655
00:28:21,110 --> 00:28:22,510
I've been to 3 hospitals,

656
00:28:23,590 --> 00:28:25,790
and they all gave me the same diagnosis.

657
00:28:27,160 --> 00:28:28,620
Go to Shanghai right away.

658
00:28:29,000 --> 00:28:30,350
I'll give you 2 phone numbers.

659
00:28:30,350 --> 00:28:31,790
They're both experts in this field.

660
00:28:31,790 --> 00:28:33,850
Make an appointment with one of them.

661
00:28:34,070 --> 00:28:34,680
Forget it.

662
00:28:36,000 --> 00:28:37,800
I don't want to waste that money.

663
00:28:38,030 --> 00:28:38,680
Hey.

664
00:28:39,590 --> 00:28:40,580
Do you even realize

665
00:28:40,580 --> 00:28:42,310
how serious your condition is?

666
00:28:42,510 --> 00:28:43,730
It's been a year

667
00:28:43,750 --> 00:28:44,790
since your last checkup.

668
00:28:44,790 --> 00:28:45,490
Do you know

669
00:28:45,520 --> 00:28:47,850
-that any moment, you could just...
-Die.

670
00:28:48,680 --> 00:28:49,480
I know.

671
00:28:51,000 --> 00:28:52,400
But can chemotherapy

672
00:28:52,480 --> 00:28:53,680
cure it at this point?

673
00:28:56,070 --> 00:28:57,350
Every doctor

674
00:28:58,920 --> 00:29:00,350
has told me clearly

675
00:29:01,240 --> 00:29:02,500
that it can't be cured.

676
00:29:03,310 --> 00:29:03,920
But...

677
00:29:05,680 --> 00:29:07,400
But it could at least

678
00:29:07,400 --> 00:29:09,270
extend your life.

679
00:29:11,350 --> 00:29:12,160
Extend it?

680
00:29:19,000 --> 00:29:20,460
I'm only 18 this year, bro.

681
00:29:22,070 --> 00:29:23,530
What good would 1 or 2 years

682
00:29:23,680 --> 00:29:24,750
do me?

683
00:29:28,590 --> 00:29:29,920
You have to at least try.

684
00:29:34,550 --> 00:29:36,510
Bro, Sis.

685
00:29:38,590 --> 00:29:39,510
I've tried.

686
00:29:55,550 --> 00:29:56,110
I'm...

687
00:29:58,640 --> 00:29:59,590
the chosen one.

688
00:30:01,590 --> 00:30:02,520
There's no cure.

689
00:30:06,400 --> 00:30:07,200
I just

690
00:30:08,160 --> 00:30:09,690
want to spend whatever time

691
00:30:10,030 --> 00:30:11,270
I have left

692
00:30:11,960 --> 00:30:14,160
without making her waste a fortune on me

693
00:30:16,000 --> 00:30:17,160
or putting myself through

694
00:30:17,160 --> 00:30:18,290
all that suffering.

695
00:30:20,000 --> 00:30:22,130
I want to use the little time I have left

696
00:30:22,680 --> 00:30:24,750
to enjoy life

697
00:30:25,790 --> 00:30:26,550
and do things

698
00:30:26,550 --> 00:30:27,880
I've never done before.

699
00:30:36,350 --> 00:30:37,810
But you can't just give up.

700
00:30:39,270 --> 00:30:41,270
You shamelessly followed me around

701
00:30:41,350 --> 00:30:42,160
because you saw

702
00:30:42,160 --> 00:30:43,590
on my resume

703
00:30:43,680 --> 00:30:46,110
that I'm an expert
in the Neurosurgical Department, right?

704
00:30:46,110 --> 00:30:47,970
You wanted me to treat you, right?

705
00:30:48,160 --> 00:30:49,310
So let me treat you.

706
00:30:53,160 --> 00:30:53,830
I did

707
00:30:53,830 --> 00:30:55,630
shamelessly follow you around.

708
00:30:56,310 --> 00:30:57,240
But like I said,

709
00:30:58,030 --> 00:30:58,920
no one can do it.

710
00:30:59,790 --> 00:31:00,720
There's no cure.

711
00:31:02,720 --> 00:31:03,720
I just...

712
00:31:05,110 --> 00:31:06,830
I just wanted to stay

713
00:31:06,830 --> 00:31:07,830
close to a doctor.

714
00:31:09,200 --> 00:31:11,130
Maybe it'd bring me some good luck.

715
00:31:11,680 --> 00:31:12,440
Or maybe one day,

716
00:31:12,440 --> 00:31:14,200
if I collapsed in the street,

717
00:31:15,270 --> 00:31:16,670
you'd be there to save me,

718
00:31:17,000 --> 00:31:17,750
right?

719
00:31:24,830 --> 00:31:25,890
Does your mom know?

720
00:31:34,550 --> 00:31:36,280
There's no need for her to know.

721
00:31:38,790 --> 00:31:39,680
I get it now.

722
00:31:40,640 --> 00:31:41,440
I was wondering why you

723
00:31:41,440 --> 00:31:43,720
always did such rebellious things before,

724
00:31:43,720 --> 00:31:44,400
always doing things

725
00:31:44,400 --> 00:31:45,790
your mom hates.

726
00:31:46,310 --> 00:31:49,000
Actually, you were deliberately
pushing her away.

727
00:31:49,000 --> 00:31:50,240
You were worried that
if she found out the truth,

728
00:31:50,240 --> 00:31:51,200
she wouldn't be able to handle it

729
00:31:51,200 --> 00:31:52,660
and would be heartbroken.

730
00:31:53,160 --> 00:31:53,960
So you deliberately

731
00:31:53,960 --> 00:31:55,360
cut ties with her, right?

732
00:32:04,790 --> 00:32:06,250
You even figured that out?

733
00:32:08,590 --> 00:32:09,790
You really are no ordinary person.

734
00:32:09,790 --> 00:32:10,680
How childish.

735
00:32:11,960 --> 00:32:12,830
She's your mom.

736
00:32:14,270 --> 00:32:14,960
No matter what you do,

737
00:32:14,960 --> 00:32:16,620
she'll still be heartbroken.

738
00:32:36,510 --> 00:32:37,720
I'm childish?

739
00:32:40,680 --> 00:32:41,310
Bro.

740
00:32:43,640 --> 00:32:44,680
Do I have a choice?

741
00:32:46,920 --> 00:32:48,270
I'm an adult.

742
00:32:49,240 --> 00:32:51,110
I can make

743
00:32:51,110 --> 00:32:52,350
my own choices.

744
00:32:54,550 --> 00:32:55,480
This is my home,

745
00:32:56,920 --> 00:32:58,920
and I've only known you
for a couple of days.

746
00:32:58,920 --> 00:32:59,750
What gives you the right

747
00:32:59,750 --> 00:33:00,880
to tell me what to do?

748
00:33:02,200 --> 00:33:04,400
Who are you to make that decision for me?

749
00:33:06,200 --> 00:33:06,960
I'm not talking to you.

750
00:33:06,960 --> 00:33:08,560
I'm going to talk to your mom.

751
00:33:11,070 --> 00:33:12,110
You have no idea

752
00:33:12,510 --> 00:33:13,680
how many tricks I pulled

753
00:33:13,680 --> 00:33:14,550
and how much effort I put in

754
00:33:14,550 --> 00:33:15,440
just to keep it from her.

755
00:33:15,440 --> 00:33:16,680
How long can you keep it a secret, huh?

756
00:33:16,680 --> 00:33:17,550
How long?

757
00:33:17,550 --> 00:33:19,480
Better to suffer a short pain
than a long one!

758
00:33:19,480 --> 00:33:21,480
But she'll find out sooner or later.

759
00:33:22,750 --> 00:33:23,550
Zhou Zheng.

760
00:33:24,030 --> 00:33:25,240
If you really treat me as your friend,

761
00:33:25,240 --> 00:33:26,100
get out of my way

762
00:33:26,110 --> 00:33:27,570
and let me talk to your mom.

763
00:33:28,310 --> 00:33:29,160
I don't want my mom

764
00:33:29,160 --> 00:33:30,420
spending my final days

765
00:33:30,750 --> 00:33:32,750
worrying about me every single day.

766
00:33:33,070 --> 00:33:33,920
You know?

767
00:33:37,750 --> 00:33:38,440
Bro.

768
00:33:39,440 --> 00:33:40,370
I'm telling you,

769
00:33:43,680 --> 00:33:45,080
this is the last decision

770
00:33:45,750 --> 00:33:47,150
I'll ever make in my life.

771
00:33:49,240 --> 00:33:50,350
My last one.

772
00:33:53,590 --> 00:33:54,550
Don't push me.

773
00:33:55,880 --> 00:33:56,830
Don't push me.

774
00:34:02,310 --> 00:34:03,880
Just respect his choice.

775
00:34:08,280 --> 00:34:09,810
What are you arguing about?

776
00:34:12,630 --> 00:34:13,670
Don't. Don't...

777
00:34:14,880 --> 00:34:15,810
I'm begging you.

778
00:34:17,550 --> 00:34:18,480
I'm begging you.

779
00:34:19,360 --> 00:34:20,400
Please.

780
00:34:21,230 --> 00:34:22,280
Please.

781
00:34:30,510 --> 00:34:32,239
What's all this arguing about?

782
00:34:32,320 --> 00:34:33,550
What are you doing?

783
00:34:34,550 --> 00:34:36,710
We didn't get to act our hearts out
on set today,

784
00:34:36,710 --> 00:34:38,110
so we're rehearsing now.

785
00:34:39,960 --> 00:34:40,760
Rehearsing?

786
00:34:40,880 --> 00:34:42,360
I-It was pretty intense.

787
00:34:44,110 --> 00:34:45,510
What's wrong? What do you need?

788
00:34:45,510 --> 00:34:46,440
Are you okay?

789
00:34:47,110 --> 00:34:48,630
What do you mean, am I okay?

790
00:34:50,630 --> 00:34:51,760
Not everything's about you, okay?

791
00:34:51,760 --> 00:34:52,320
You...

792
00:34:52,870 --> 00:34:54,590
-Let's rehearse for a little longer.
-Come on. Get out.

793
00:34:54,590 --> 00:34:55,850
Why are you pushing me?

794
00:34:56,920 --> 00:34:58,580
Don't come over for no reason.

795
00:35:13,590 --> 00:35:19,910
[Fire Evacuation Plan]

796
00:35:22,650 --> 00:35:28,410
[Storefront for Lease]

797
00:35:49,840 --> 00:35:50,630
Can't sleep?

798
00:35:53,070 --> 00:35:54,400
I see you can't, either.

799
00:36:00,360 --> 00:36:01,960
How could this happen to him?

800
00:36:03,670 --> 00:36:05,000
He's still so young.

801
00:36:06,030 --> 00:36:07,030
You must have seen

802
00:36:08,320 --> 00:36:10,120
more cases like this than I have.

803
00:36:24,360 --> 00:36:25,760
There's a hospital in Guilin

804
00:36:25,760 --> 00:36:27,760
that asked me to go for an interview.

805
00:36:27,800 --> 00:36:29,060
I'm leaving tomorrow.

806
00:36:37,840 --> 00:36:40,840
You just found out that he's sick,
and you're leaving?

807
00:36:44,760 --> 00:36:46,760
What's the point of staying anyway?

808
00:36:47,840 --> 00:36:48,710
He's right.

809
00:36:50,030 --> 00:36:51,560
His illness can't be cured,

810
00:36:52,480 --> 00:36:54,410
and that day could come at any time.

811
00:36:54,840 --> 00:36:56,640
I don't want to see him like that.

812
00:36:57,550 --> 00:36:58,880
While we're not that close,

813
00:36:58,880 --> 00:37:00,360
the sooner I leave, the better.

814
00:37:00,360 --> 00:37:01,820
You're just running away—

815
00:37:02,070 --> 00:37:03,550
running as far away as possible.

816
00:37:03,550 --> 00:37:05,750
When faced with a problem I can't solve,

817
00:37:05,920 --> 00:37:07,580
what else can I do but run away?

818
00:37:17,880 --> 00:37:18,710
Running away

819
00:37:18,960 --> 00:37:20,230
will become a habit.

820
00:37:23,280 --> 00:37:24,740
And eventually, even when

821
00:37:25,230 --> 00:37:26,070
a problem can be solved,

822
00:37:26,070 --> 00:37:27,470
you'll still run from it.

823
00:37:51,840 --> 00:37:53,370
In my career, the first time

824
00:37:54,250 --> 00:37:55,580
I ever had a patient

825
00:37:55,600 --> 00:37:56,920
die in front of me

826
00:37:58,880 --> 00:38:00,030
was when...

827
00:38:00,880 --> 00:38:02,360
When I was an intern.

828
00:38:02,920 --> 00:38:04,440
It was an old man.

829
00:38:06,360 --> 00:38:07,230
My attending told me

830
00:38:07,230 --> 00:38:08,150
he'd come in

831
00:38:08,150 --> 00:38:09,630
every winter,

832
00:38:10,960 --> 00:38:13,560
and he'd eat 2 servings of rice rolls
every day.

833
00:38:15,480 --> 00:38:17,410
But during the few days I was there,

834
00:38:18,710 --> 00:38:20,710
he could only manage 1 serving a day.

835
00:38:22,400 --> 00:38:23,630
My attending said

836
00:38:26,510 --> 00:38:28,040
he didn't have long to live,

837
00:38:28,670 --> 00:38:29,800
but he did nothing.

838
00:38:31,480 --> 00:38:32,410
And sure enough,

839
00:38:34,230 --> 00:38:35,280
a few days later,

840
00:38:35,880 --> 00:38:37,320
the old man passed away.

841
00:38:39,880 --> 00:38:40,670
You see,

842
00:38:41,070 --> 00:38:42,670
that's how things often are.

843
00:38:43,480 --> 00:38:46,030
Sometimes, you already know
how things will end,

844
00:38:46,030 --> 00:38:48,830
but there's still nothing you can do
to prevent it.

845
00:38:49,480 --> 00:38:50,630
This is true of life,

846
00:38:51,070 --> 00:38:52,730
and it's true of death as well.

847
00:38:55,030 --> 00:38:55,880
You're right.

848
00:38:58,880 --> 00:39:00,030
Everyone dies.

849
00:39:02,890 --> 00:39:04,410
But that doesn't mean

850
00:39:04,440 --> 00:39:06,370
there's nothing we can do about it.

851
00:39:07,030 --> 00:39:08,880
Someone has to do something, right?

852
00:39:08,880 --> 00:39:10,320
Even if we know
we can't change the outcome,

853
00:39:10,320 --> 00:39:11,480
we should still try.

854
00:39:14,670 --> 00:39:16,870
Otherwise, what's the point of living?

855
00:39:24,760 --> 00:39:26,620
Is that what you wanted to tell me?

856
00:39:30,070 --> 00:39:30,880
It's not.

857
00:39:50,710 --> 00:39:51,640
Liu Zhengliang.

858
00:39:57,480 --> 00:39:58,920
This is my first time

859
00:40:00,670 --> 00:40:02,870
spending New Year's Eve away from home.

860
00:40:16,920 --> 00:40:17,980
The New Year's bell

861
00:40:18,000 --> 00:40:19,760
is about to ring.

862
00:40:19,920 --> 00:40:22,590
Let's count down together!

863
00:40:22,840 --> 00:40:23,710
Ten.

864
00:40:23,960 --> 00:40:24,840
Nine.

865
00:40:25,070 --> 00:40:25,960
Eight.

866
00:40:26,070 --> 00:40:26,960
Seven.

867
00:40:27,230 --> 00:40:28,110
Six.

868
00:40:28,320 --> 00:40:29,150
Five.

869
00:40:29,400 --> 00:40:30,150
Four.

870
00:40:30,440 --> 00:40:31,110
Three.

871
00:40:31,480 --> 00:40:32,150
Two.

872
00:40:32,400 --> 00:40:33,480
One.

873
00:40:33,800 --> 00:40:35,550
Happy New Year!

874
00:40:35,710 --> 00:40:36,880
Happy New Year!

875
00:40:39,410 --> 00:40:46,540
♪ It's only after something is lost
that we begin to see ♪

876
00:40:48,350 --> 00:40:54,130
♪ But some things can never be undone ♪

877
00:40:57,330 --> 00:41:03,720
♪ When snowflakes cover
all our yesterdays ♪

878
00:41:04,970 --> 00:41:11,000
♪ Perhaps it's best
we leave the words unsaid ♪

879
00:41:14,860 --> 00:41:22,020
♪ We were once someone else ♪

880
00:41:23,690 --> 00:41:29,740
♪ Then, one day,
we found our truest selves ♪

881
00:41:26,280 --> 00:41:27,070
Check out, please.

882
00:41:27,070 --> 00:41:27,710
Okay.

883
00:41:32,580 --> 00:41:39,490
♪ Turns out,
you don't have to fall apart ♪

884
00:41:32,630 --> 00:41:34,110
Has my friend left?

885
00:41:35,000 --> 00:41:37,030
She checked out early in the morning.

886
00:41:37,030 --> 00:41:38,230
Here's your deposit.

887
00:41:40,230 --> 00:41:47,820
♪ To deserve a fresh start ♪

888
00:41:48,000 --> 00:41:48,960
Thank you.

889
00:41:52,110 --> 00:41:54,640
Thank you for
hanging around with Zhou Zheng.

890
00:41:55,360 --> 00:41:57,920
My son doesn't have many friends.

891
00:41:58,800 --> 00:42:00,760
He was really happy
spending these past few days

892
00:42:00,760 --> 00:42:01,800
with you.

893
00:42:02,920 --> 00:42:03,710
Thank you.

894
00:42:14,400 --> 00:42:15,400
This is my number.

895
00:42:15,920 --> 00:42:17,190
If you have anything you want to ask,

896
00:42:17,190 --> 00:42:18,120
call me anytime.

897
00:42:26,000 --> 00:42:32,750
♪ Not every goodbye is meant to
erase the past ♪

898
00:42:34,770 --> 00:42:41,730
♪ At least we met with open hearts ♪

899
00:42:36,110 --> 00:42:39,280
[May Your Journey Be Safe
and the New Year Bring Joy to Your Door]

900
00:42:43,470 --> 00:42:46,270
♪ When life stretches on for so long ♪

901
00:42:47,010 --> 00:42:50,800
♪ Not every story needs a perfect ending ♪

902
00:42:51,410 --> 00:42:59,540
♪ Maybe walking side by side
for a while is enough ♪

903
00:43:00,600 --> 00:43:11,570
♪ I'll keep those words we never
got to say in my heart ♪
